# AGENTS.md hierarchy (Cursor)

Cursor injects the repo-root `AGENTS.md`. Also apply Codex's extra layers:

1. If `~/.codex/AGENTS.override.md` or `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` exists, read it as global defaults. Project files override it.
2. Read every `AGENTS.md` from the repo root down to files you edit. Closer files win on conflict.
3. In this repo, `docs/AGENTS.md` applies when working under `docs/`.
4. Follow `@path` includes in those files. Do not scan `~/Library` or `/Volumes` to discover them.
5. Add a nested `AGENTS.md` only when a folder has durable distinct ownership or workflow.
